{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations","id":954255,"title":"ALL THE POPULATIONS","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-20T00:09:38-07:00","id":954255,"title":"ALL THE POPULATIONS","content":"There have been a lot of &quot;what is the population (rate) of X&quot; posts lately. It occurs to me that it would be good to combine all the Awakened Being populations in one place. The following are my personal preferences--actually they are my preferences when taken individually, with a given splat assumed as the focus of the game being run. I deemphasize the groups I'm not running at a given time, which usually means they are less in number than what they would be if I were running them. Also, if I'm being honest, I just produce an amount of whatever splat makes sense to the plot as I go along. This was an amusing exercise though.<br /> <br /> Vampires (Cainite)--1 in 50,000. It's a nice compromise between the 1 in 100,000 of OWoD and the 1 in 10,000 of NWoD. It doesn't seem like a lot, but I assume vampires don't bother with towns or cities under 300,000 (where about 5/6 of humans live) and that most of East Asia is kept Cainite-free by the Cathayans. Both these factors drive up Cainite-per-person in the places actually inhabited by Cainites. I like a higher vampire population than given in OWoD because vampires are the main reason the WoD is the WoD. They are literally the reason it sucks so much.<br /> <br /> Werewolves--1 in 400,000. This sounds like a small number and it is. But there is only one actual wolf for every 35,000 people approximately, and it would be weird to me if there were more than one werewolf per 10 wolves. Also Wolves have a limited range in the world, and I imagine werewolves mostly keep to that range.<br /> <br /> Mages--1 in 200,000. This is a pretty small number when you consider that this includes Technocrats who barely seem like mages at all. I like the number being small, though. Mages dynamically warp reality at will. It seems safe to say that their influence is disproportionate.<br /> <br /> Wraiths--1 in 200 not including Drones. I know the books add a zero to the numerator of that, but I can't bring myself to accept such a high number. Even with the Shroud, that many Wraiths would probably have been officially and definitively discovered by humans. 35 million wraiths is enough for them to have the complex and fairly autonomous societies they are portrayed as having.<br /> <br /> Changelings--1 in 10,000. It's hard to come up with a good number for Changelings. On the one hand they are a dying race of otherworldly beings living among people whose very unbelief unravels their existence. On the other hand they have a stratified social structure with fae courts and working classes. 700,000 seems like the minimum required to maintain some semblance of that, assuming a lot of those titles are just bluster. Too much higher than that, and our world would probably look a lot different than the one we live in.<br /> <br /> Demons--Hell if I know. According to Renaissance era demonologists there are anywhere from about four million to about 130 million. Either seems like a lot. But then not only a small fraction of them would have made it to Earth. There should probably be fewer Fallen than vampires if both exist in the same setting. Maybe one for every 5 vampires, so one in every quarter million humans?<br /> <br /> Kue Jin--1 in 300,000. They're only in East Asia and some East Asian diasporas, and I imagine them being less common per human than Cainites because they don't reproduce (other Kue Jin anyway).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T01:18:30-07:00","id":954269,"title":"","content":"Sometime in the next week or so, I'll post some very rough demographic breakdowns. As it stands my figures don't really go into the ratio of creatures to humans, but they do contain ballpark estimates for the proportion of clans, tribes, etc. If I don't, someone PM me until I do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T01:47:16-07:00","id":954277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations#post954255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Demons--Hell if I know. According to Renaissance era demonologists there are anywhere from about four million to about 130 million. Either seems like a lot. But then not only a small fraction of them would have made it to Earth. There should probably be fewer Fallen than vampires if both exist in the same setting. Maybe one for every 5 vampires, so one in every quarter million humans?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to imagine actual Fallens - demons who are Fallen Angels that revolted against God - are rare compared to demons who to demons that other game lines mention (that might come from the Astral Plane or from outside reality. Or Banes or other Wyrm-related spirits). Or possibly it is extremely rare that such a Fallen Angel possesses a human.<br /> This is because I consider the way they can Pact humans - and how it can be done more or less unknowingly, how it is unbreakable unless the demon makes a mistake, and how they can then ravage those humans for faith if they get uppity - to be both horrific and potentially overpowered. Even if we assume that mortals with Faith potential are rare; Faith potential can be nurtured. They can also walk around in their human form as if nothing supernatural was going on. So Fallens - possibly served by other types of demons - would be the terrible rarity that other supernaturals might sometimes stumble upon. They might even have adopted an approach where they take over the 300,000 population and lower population cities that you mentioned Cainites aren't interested in.<br /> Considering this, I'd put them at 400,000-500,000 or perhaps even 1 in a million humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 08-20-2016, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T02:08:21-07:00","id":954281,"title":"","content":"Depending on how one views the count given in various Demon supplements, there should be between 2,002,204 - 30,000,000 maximum demons. Either end of that is likely poetic rather than especially accurate. This figure of course has no real help in determining how many are active, but it does tell us there must be <i>less</i> than the high end maximum. If, for argument's sake, every demon suddenly incarned out of the Abyss, at the low end it'd be 1 in every 4000 humans. At the high end, 1 for every 234 humans.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T07:50:50-07:00","id":954378,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Kue Jin--1 in 300,000. They're only in East Asia and some East Asian diasporas, and I imagine them being less common per human than Cainites because they don't reproduce (other Kue Jin anyway). </div> </div> </div>The Requirement to be a KJ is roughly the same as being a Wraith, so while Kindred might have the embrace something like the Killing Fields massively grew the KJ population.<br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly though the X supernatural to number is really kind of a shitty way of dealing with them because like people supernaturals Clump. There may in theory be 70000 or so vampires of all shapes and flavours but there are going to be vast swaths of rural areas that are going to be under represented and tourist towns that are going to be over represented.<br /> <br /> Werecreatures are going to be focused around Caerns which may or may not have a connection to human life.<br /> <br /> Mages are going to have a similar setup on Nodes but are also able to more readily spread out and maintain a &quot;society&quot; Mages don't need to have 30 guy in a city to have a Chantry a cabal might be spread out across half the mid atlantic without much issue.<br /> <br /> Wraiths well they are going to clump at cities.. and points of horror. Gettysburg only has roughly 7000 or so living people.. by the 1 in 200 rule there should be only 35 ghosts including drones, and that would't quite work.<br /> <br /> Changelings are going to reasonably be focused around Glamour. Places with many freeholds and glens are going to be far more Changeling happy. <br /> <br /> <br /> So nothing is ever going to live up to broad statistics just pick what works for story. I'm personally good with a rule of thumb Wraiths&gt;Mortal+&gt;Changelings&gt;Vampires&gt;Werewolves&gt;Ma ges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T08:36:04-07:00","id":954407,"title":"","content":"Generally, the overall numbers don't matter much, but for world building I use an old Census file I had found online and saved. It listed which numbers were canonically verified and which were wholly made up. The numbers have probably changed in the past 15 years, but it still serves well enough.<br /> For my games:<br /> Vampires: 1:100,000 (including KJ), 1:50,000 outside of Asia and Africa<br /> Garou: 13-14k total<br /> Mages: about 11,000 total between all faction and in and out of the Umbra<br /> Wraiths: A lot more than everyone else. (millions-billions)<br /> Changelings: 1:20,000<br /> Demons: I never cared<br /> KuieJin: about 21,000<br /> Mummies: rare-ish. never bothered with a number (maybe a couple of thousand total)<br /> <br /> Fomori: 1 per shifter at any given moment (so about 47,000-ish)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T08:51:49-07:00","id":954415,"title":"","content":"I tend to go with the following numbers as proportion of the global mortal population (though recent discussions have changed my position on some of the populations).<br /> <br /> Kindred: 1:100,000<br /> Kuei-jin: 1:100,000<br /> Wraith: 1:20<br /> Fera (including Garou): 1:200,000<br /> Kinfolk (including Garou): 1:2,000<br /> Mages: 1:1,000,000<br /> Sorcerers (practitioners of Mythic Numina, Psychic Numina, Scientific Numina, True Faith, etc): 1:500<br /> Chanelings: 1:20,000<br /> Kinain: 1:2,000<br /> Demons: Who cares? Anyone smart exorcises them or kills them on sight.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T20:04:54-07:00","id":954763,"title":"","content":"Mummies--I remember there being only about a hundred in the whole world. Unless you go by MtR which everyone else but me does, in which case it might be different. I use the original version that's like 60 pages and has a psychedelic cover. Maybe not the best choice, but definitely the grooviest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T21:13:29-07:00","id":954796,"title":"","content":"I do like the 2nd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T07:51:21-07:00","id":954947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations#post954255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolves--1 in 400,000. This sounds like a small number and it is. But there is only one actual wolf for every 35,000 people approximately, and it would be weird to me if there were more than one werewolf per 10 wolves. Also Wolves have a limited range in the world, and I imagine werewolves mostly keep to that range.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There are more wolves in the WoD than in real life. Paradoxical in some ways regarding the theme, but if you're going for massive cities separated by a vast and scary wilderness, there's more room for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T08:19:26-07:00","id":954957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=954947#post954947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are more wolves in the WoD than in real life. Paradoxical in some ways regarding the theme, but if you're going for massive cities separated by a vast and scary wilderness, there's more room for them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are explicitly still Hakken Wolfkin in the world of Darkness...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T10:02:33-07:00","id":955003,"title":"","content":"Yes, in Hokkaido, though the wild wolves of Japan are extinct. I do not terribly care about narrative fluff, you cannot support a population of over 7 billion humans cannot exist if there is more wilderness. You either have to have reduced wilderness or reduced human population because it is zero sum game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T11:24:34-07:00","id":955033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=955003#post955003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, in Hokkaido, though the wild wolves of Japan are extinct. I do not terribly care about narrative fluff, you cannot support a population of over 7 billion humans cannot exist if there is more wilderness. You either have to have reduced wilderness or reduced human population because it is zero sum game.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a make believe world. You can have both with no problem at all. No player is going to care if the wilds are an extra hour longer to get through","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T11:30:15-07:00","id":955037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=955003#post955003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, in Hokkaido, though the wild wolves of Japan are extinct. I do not terribly care about narrative fluff, you cannot support a population of over 7 billion humans cannot exist if there is more wilderness. You either have to have reduced wilderness or reduced human population because it is zero sum game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Japan is bigger? While still having the same shape. Or a different shape perhaps? :-P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:44:33-07:00","id":955101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=955003#post955003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, in Hokkaido, though the wild wolves of Japan are extinct. I do not terribly care about narrative fluff, you cannot support a population of over 7 billion humans cannot exist if there is more wilderness. You either have to have reduced wilderness or reduced human population because it is zero sum game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In a reality that's stable and objective presumably yes. What that has to do with the World of darkness..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:55:27-07:00","id":955106,"title":"","content":"If it is a dark reflection of the real world, then it has to resemble our world, just with hidden elements. Otherwise, it might as well be Middle Earth...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T13:26:37-07:00","id":955131,"title":"","content":"Somewhere in some book Demon: The Fallen defines exactly how many Elohim there were. I can't find it, but I do recall the number being in the ballpark of 100.000.000, with some more ones added to the mix. Something like 100.100.001 or something.<br /> <br /> A third of those rebelled against God. After some number of casualties the survivors were locked away into the Abyss, with the weakest of their number starting to escape.<br /> <br /> Other numbers aren't given, so we don't know the casualty rates. If we go by a 50% casualty rate, and that only the weakest 1% has escaped we're looking at about 166.666 Fallen currently in the world, a fitting number given the subject matter. This would meant that the rate is about 1:42.000. But once again, this is mere guesswork.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T13:29:08-07:00","id":955133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=955106#post955106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it is a dark reflection of the real world, then it has to resemble our world, just with hidden elements. Otherwise, it might as well be Middle Earth...</div> </div> </div> </div>There is certainly space between resembling our world and middle earth. Distances don't have to be exact. It's a game not a geography test.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T15:33:16-07:00","id":955237,"title":"","content":"Middle Earth is partially based on the Earth (thus the name), so there is less than you think. And I think that it weakens the based premise of the world of darkness for the surface appearances of the world of darkness to be different than the surface appearance of our world. Anyway, every book in the world of darkness keeps the maps and distances the same as they are in our world, so its geography reflects our Earth perfectly. If you want a different world of darkness though, feel free, but it is not canon, it is just another fantasy world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T15:42:14-07:00","id":955247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=955237#post955237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Middle Earth is partially based on the Earth (thus the name), so there is less than you think. And I think that it weakens the based premise of the world of darkness for the surface appearances of the world of darkness to be different than the surface appearance of our world. Anyway, every book in the world of darkness keeps the maps and distances the same as they are in our world, so its geography reflects our Earth perfectly. If you want a different world of darkness though, feel free, but it is not canon, it is just another fantasy world.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> All of canada is within 2 hours helecopter Fight from Toronto, it says so in werewolf book.<br /> <br /> <br /> More seriously the fact that reality itself seems to fluxate and you actually could travel to places like Prester John's Kingdom in the past says things may not be as stable as in our world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T16:27:28-07:00","id":955272,"title":"","content":"The majority of the population of Canada does live within two hours helicopter flight of Toronto. If you have subjective and plastic geography, it is not the world of darkness, it is just some subjectivistic fantasy created for power gamers by power gamers. I prefer to play the world of darkness as an overlay over our world, our world plus the supernatural, with the subjective BS being the rationalizations of Mages who are just as deluded as the Marauders that they oppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T17:21:55-07:00","id":955309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=955272#post955272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have subjective and plastic geography, it is not the world of darkness, it is just some subjectivistic fantasy created for power gamers by power gamers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really have no idea how not caring about specific geography makes anyone a power gamer. That statement is utterly ridiculous.<br /> To have a higher population with more expensive wildness all you need to do is have cities more densely packed, as is implied. <br /> Or just not worry about the precise number of miles between cities. This is a game. The point is to have fun. Wether it's 225 miles from one city to another or 250 won't ruin the world, I promise you.<br /> Either solution works fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T17:25:31-07:00","id":955310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=955237#post955237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Middle Earth is partially based on the Earth (thus the name), so there is less than you think. And I think that it weakens the based premise of the world of darkness for the surface appearances of the world of darkness to be different than the surface appearance of our world. Anyway, every book in the world of darkness keeps the maps and distances the same as they are in our world, so its geography reflects our Earth perfectly. If you want a different world of darkness though, feel free, but it is not canon, it is just another fantasy world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Middle Earth is a fucking flat fantasy world, not a conspiracy-wracked gothic reflection of the real world that packs more people into cities than the real world does. Suburbs are presumably fewer in number, replaced in most locales by more heavily-built up urban blocks, and &quot;rural&quot; areas are closer than they would be in real life. Everyone is bunched up and uncomfortable, but unwilling to try their luck living in the sticks, where rumors of serial killers and wild dogs abound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 08-21-2016, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T20:18:35-07:00","id":955381,"title":"","content":"It is not the cities that matter, it is the cultivated land. What will people eat if you have more wilderness replacing farmland and pastures?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T20:43:13-07:00","id":955389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=955381#post955381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is not the cities that matter, it is the cultivated land. What will people eat if you have more wilderness replacing farmland and pastures?</div> </div> </div> </div>That will never come up in any world of darkness game (at least any that I have ever run or player in) so it doesn't matter. You are worrying about details that make zero difference.<br /> <br /> The people will eat whatever you as a ST day they eat. If it does matter to you that much, have the lack of food add to your WoD. It would fit right in with the rest of the oppressive setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T21:46:28-07:00","id":955421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=955381#post955381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is not the cities that matter, it is the cultivated land. What will people eat if you have more wilderness replacing farmland and pastures?</div> </div> </div> </div>The US, at least, doesn't use much land as-is for farming, and doesn't need to, courtesy of industrial operations and greater comparative yields per unit. The amount probably wouldn't change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T22:47:46-07:00","id":955441,"title":"","content":"The USA has over 4 million square kilometers of agricultural land, over 40% of the area of the nation, so we have quite a bit. Of course, that is a lower percentage than Western Europe, but we have 60% the population and export 40% of the grain that we produce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T03:06:40-07:00","id":955497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=955381#post955381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is not the cities that matter, it is the cultivated land. What will people eat if you have more wilderness replacing farmland and pastures?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Over history we've become more efficient with Farmland, presume a slightly higher level of agricultural technology, because real actual fucking technomagick exists..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T04:44:27-07:00","id":955520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=954415#post954415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to go with the following numbers as proportion of the global mortal population (though recent discussions have changed my position on some of the populations).<br /> <br /> Kindred: 1:100,000<br /> Kuei-jin: 1:100,000<br /> Wraith: 1:20<br /> Fera (including Garou): 1:200,000<br /> Kinfolk (including Garou): 1:2,000<br /> Mages: 1:1,000,000<br /> Sorcerers (practitioners of Mythic Numina, Psychic Numina, Scientific Numina, True Faith, etc): 1:500<br /> Chanelings: 1:20,000<br /> Kinain: 1:2,000<br /> Demons: Who cares? Anyone smart exorcises them or kills them on sight.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> mages numbers were retconned to &quot;one in 200.000 to 1 in 250.000&quot; because writers realised the previous was to few.<br /> <br /> as for fera. i seem to recall reading that werewolves were &quot;1 in 500.000&quot; and they made up half of the fera . so the fera total being 1 in 250.000?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T07:02:39-07:00","id":955554,"title":"","content":"Yes, I know, but I consider the retconned Mage number too high and the retconned Fera number too low, so I go with different numbers (I do the same with the Kinain, Kinfolk, and Sorcerer numbers). It is less important what the canon populations are and, especially in crossover games, what will prevent wholesale genocide. In addition, I tend to think that all Mages are insane, it is just that the ones afflicted with Quiet are strong enough to change local Reality to reflect their insanity, so making them number 7,500 worldwide prevents them from being the dominant supernatural force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:37:04-07:00","id":955681,"title":"","content":"Just to put the wolf thing in perspective for Japan, only 15 percent of the area is used for farmlands and rural Japan is rapidly depopulating. The exitinction of the wolf was not driven IRL by population pressure but rather active destruction by humans. Even then there is some arguments for the continued existence of Wolves in Japan(though this is fringe but less so than bigfoot).<br /> <br /> So there's no reason Japan WOULDN&quot;T have room for hidden Wolves, especially with werewolves actively protecting them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:47:31-07:00","id":955696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=955554#post955554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In addition, I tend to think that all Mages are insane, it is just that the ones afflicted with Quiet are strong enough to change local Reality to reflect their insanity, so making them number 7,500 worldwide prevents them from being the dominant supernatural force.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you could simply make it so that Marauders (if that is who you mean with &quot;change local reality&quot;) don't get the Marauder bubble as anything more than a mind effect that usually ends up driving people insane. So Marauder doesn't get to morph everyone around him into dinosaurs or turn any and all bricks into jelly, just because &quot;he is a Marauder&quot;. It just seems like it, because people suffer from both hallucinations and adopting the outlook of the Marauder; they also, if anyone needs proof that it's for real, do it for real.<br /> The real danger of Marauders would be that their mind-warping can create reality zones that would allow them to cast their mad Magicks as coincidental; they could also, in one way or another, gather disturbingly many people who count as acolytes. But it would need time to set it up, and certainly would not be as powerful and uncounterable as the current Marauders.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T11:55:57-07:00","id":955761,"title":"","content":"According to Wikipedia there are 200.000 gray wolves in the world. If the Garou population is proportionate to this there are... well, not a lot of Garou in the world.<br /> <br /> So either there are not a lot of Garou or there are far more wolves in the World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T12:15:31-07:00","id":955772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=955761#post955761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to Wikipedia there are 200.000 gray wolves in the world. If the Garou population is proportionate to this there are... well, not a lot of Garou in the world.<br /> <br /> So either there are not a lot of Garou or there are far more wolves in the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most Garou are Homids nowadays (about 2/3s). So the overall Garou population shouldn't be proportional to the worldwide wolf population. At least that's my take on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T12:28:04-07:00","id":955781,"title":"","content":"Well, something like 1/7th of werewolves are lupus, so that would be around 2,000 Garou. If you go with a 1:10 ratio of lupus to wolf kinfolk, that would be around 10% of the estimated global wolf population (either observed or hidden, it really does not matter for these purposes), so you do not need to change Garou or wolf populations. I would suggest that the same circumstances that are endangering wolves, expanding human consumption of the Earth's resources, also contribute to the decline of Garou populations because they are fighting those circumstances and, for the most part, losing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T12:31:22-07:00","id":955788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=955761#post955761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to Wikipedia there are 200.000 gray wolves in the world. If the Garou population is proportionate to this there are... well, not a lot of Garou in the world.<br /> <br /> So either there are not a lot of Garou or there are far more wolves in the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Real world doesn't have werewolves keeping that number up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T12:36:21-07:00","id":955802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=955788#post955788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Real world doesn't have werewolves keeping that number up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, so there should be far more wolves in the World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T13:23:54-07:00","id":955841,"title":"","content":"What would they eat? Part of the problem with maintaining wolf populations is not the land, it is the availability of prey, as humans have a tendency of killing large herbivores for food and sport. It is one of the reasons why all large predators have difficulty (the other being that humans hunt the large predators for sport). However, you do not need more wolves to support the Garou population, the current wolf population seems sufficient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T14:15:36-07:00","id":955885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=955841#post955841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would they eat? Part of the problem with maintaining wolf populations is not the land, it is the availability of prey, as humans have a tendency of killing large herbivores for food and sport. It is one of the reasons why all large predators have difficulty (the other being that humans hunt the large predators for sport). However, you do not need more wolves to support the Garou population, the current wolf population seems sufficient.</div> </div> </div> </div>Litterally magic cheating. Plus I feel your Garou numbers do a disservice to the &quot;islands of safety&quot; Vampire theme.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T14:28:06-07:00","id":955890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=955781#post955781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, something like 1/7th of werewolves are lupus, so that would be around 2,000 Garou. If you go with a 1:10 ratio of lupus to wolf kinfolk, that would be around 10% of the estimated global wolf population (either observed or hidden, it really does not matter for these purposes), so you do not need to change Garou or wolf populations. I would suggest that the same circumstances that are endangering wolves, expanding human consumption of the Earth's resources, also contribute to the decline of Garou populations because they are fighting those circumstances and, for the most part, losing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is the 1/7 ratio from? I always used 25% for the # of Garou that were Lupus. Homid/Lupus/Metis I divide up 67/25/8. Your numbers put at least 80% of Garou being Homid which seems a bit high.<br /> Also, and admittedly this only impacts the overall number a little. It is worth counting the non gray wolf populations of Garou. Jackals for the Striders, Dingos for some Australian Garou and the African Wild Dogs to make up some number of Lupus Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T16:01:36-07:00","id":955949,"title":"","content":"Bone Gnawed Revised, p. 42, under the Lupus section. It specifies that one-seventh of Garou are Lupus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T18:12:14-07:00","id":956042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=955949#post955949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bone Gnawed Revised, p. 42, under the Lupus section. It specifies that one-seventh of Garou are Lupus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. Thanks for the page reference. Just looked up some other places and W20 and the Revised ST Handbook both say 1/8 so it seems the writers didn't really agree anyway. I'll go ahead and continue to use 25% for Lupus. I don't see the point in having Garou have around 85% of them be Homid.<br /> <br /> The ST Revised Handbook also has a section on Demographics (starting on page 32) which states that Ananasi and Ratkin are both equal to or possibly more than the Garou in numbers, for what it's worth. It then lists which Fera have the numbers of a &quot;healthy tribe&quot; (Bastet, Corax, Mokole, Rokea, Nagah, Kitsune and Kumo) and which Fera have &quot;painfully few&quot; members (Nuwisha, Gurahl, Same-Bito and Ajaba). The Kumo are listed here separately from the Ananasi, with the Kumo being in the healthy tribe numbers, which is why I put the Ananasi total as being equal (or higher) than Garou usually.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T19:48:46-07:00","id":956090,"title":"","content":"Thank you. That suggests that the Fera may have a population of 1:100,000 (1:500,000 Ananasi, 1:500,000 Garou, 1:500,000 Ratkin, and 1:250,000 other Fera). I would think that each of the healthy tribes have an average population of 1:1,750,000.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T08:08:53-07:00","id":956322,"title":"","content":"More demographics will be coming in the next few days. These are very rough figures and should only be considered to be loosely representative of rough breakdown by proportion, not of total populations. For an example of how rough this is, there are over 3000 indicators of direct sire-childe first-generation relationships, and in those cases my papers usually only list the clan once rather than both times.<br /> <br /> From a pool of 8801 entries, the clans make up the following proportions:<br /> Assamite: 4%<br /> Brujah: 10%<br /> Caitiff: 3%<br /> Cappadocian: 2%<br /> Gangrel: 8%<br /> Giovanni: 5%<br /> Lasombra: 6%<br /> Malkavian: 7%<br /> Nosferatu: 8%<br /> Ravnos: 3%<br /> Setite: 4%<br /> Toreador: 9%<br /> Tremere: 9%<br /> Tzimisce: 5%<br /> Ventrue: 11%<br /> Salubri: 1%<br /> Gargoyles: 1%<br /> Samedi: 1%<br /> Laibon (all lines): 1%<br /> All other bloodlines: 2%<br /> There is 1 ghoul for every 12 vampires recorded, and 1 in 10 vampires are diablerists.<br /> <br /> There are 3600 lineages that exend to first-degree relations (sire-childe), 1101 that extend to sire-grandchilde, 312 that extend to sire-ggc, 108 that extend to sire-gggc, 42 that extend to sire-ggggc, 10 that extend to sire-gggggc, and 2 that extend all the way to sire-ggggggc. That one is enough steps for, without diablerie or other shenanigans, one of those 2 to be 10th generation with an unbroken line from their antediluvian progenitor, with only one mention of clan in that entire list. In the worst case scenario, all ~5000 of those entries could significantly skew the results.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T10:17:42-07:00","id":956396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=956322#post956322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brujah: 10%<br /> <br /> Ventrue: 11%</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it just me, or is it weird to see more Ventrue than Brujah?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T10:28:32-07:00","id":956400,"title":"","content":"Not really. Ventrue often have large broods and a lower mortality rate than Brujah do. There are also more Ventrue princes controlling the right to sire than there are Brujah.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> To illustrate, when it comes to princes and other rulers (barons, anarch barons, bishops etc haven't been included because it's 4:30AM), and with the caveat there are many duplicate entries, entries span the entire history of the cainites without discrimination, and some princes do not have a known clan. Percentages are of princes with known clans / princes (including unknown clan)<br /> Ventrue 37% / 20%<br /> Toreador 15%/8%<br /> Brujah 10%/6%<br /> Lasombra 10%/5%<br /> Malkavians 6%/3%<br /> Tremere 5%/2%<br /> Nosferatu 4%/2%<br /> Tzimisce 3%/2%<br /> Gangrel 3%/2%<br /> All others with known clans: 7%/5% (with 45% of the total number being of unknown clan)<br /> <br /> As you can see, the Ventrue make up a sizeable plurality of princes, and while the Brujah hold their own compared to the other major clans, they don't quite hold a candle to the primacy of the children of Veddartha.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5307,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","user":"loomer","date":". 08-23-2016, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T11:29:02-07:00","id":956448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=956400#post956400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. Ventrue often have large broods and a lower mortality rate than Brujah do. There are also more Ventrue princes controlling the right to sire than there are Brujah.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ventrue are also, arguably, a lot pickier in who they embrace than Brujah (or Gangrel for that matter). I've always viewed Ventrue numbers as being less than either of those clans.<br /> <br /> Your numbers are from compiling all of the NPCs written up from books? Mind you, regardless I am interested in seeing the numbers according to others either way and where they numbers come from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T12:13:03-07:00","id":956482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=956396#post956396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it just me, or is it weird to see more Ventrue than Brujah?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are no Ventrue, only Independents and Sabbat pretending to be Ventrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T18:59:16-07:00","id":956690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=956448#post956448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ventrue are also, arguably, a lot pickier in who they embrace than Brujah (or Gangrel for that matter). I've always viewed Ventrue numbers as being less than either of those clans.<br /> <br /> Your numbers are from compiling all of the NPCs written up from books? Mind you, regardless I am interested in seeing the numbers according to others either way and where they numbers come from.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's correct. They come from reading each and every book and other canonical property of the various game lines and entering every specific supernatural entity, including those without names, into a document. At present there are over 15,000 entries for vampire alone, and a total of .~34,000 entries across all game lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T19:48:57-07:00","id":956709,"title":"","content":"Interesting. I still think Brujah should be more populous than Ventrue. I think writers just feel the need to put Ventrue in more places since they're on typically on charge of everything.<br /> <br /> I am very interested to see the rest of the demographics from your project. Even if I disagree, it's awesome to see this work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T20:38:03-07:00","id":956750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=956709#post956709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. I still think Brujah should be more populous than Ventrue. I think writers just feel the need to put Ventrue in more places since they're on typically on charge of everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, the difference between the Brujah and the Ventrue isn't that there are fewer Brujah; it is that the Ventrue in a chronicle have <i>names. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T20:41:40-07:00","id":956754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=956750#post956750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, the difference between the Brujah and the Ventrue isn't that there are fewer Brujah; it is that the Ventrue in a chronicle have <i>names. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>That actually makes sense \u263a","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T23:42:08-07:00","id":956819,"title":"","content":"Today, let's look at the known figures - with the caveats of duplicates etc; not comprehensive, etc, etc - for Werewolf. There is also going to be a bias towards more 'interesting' populations in the books, and their regional focuses mean that figures may not apply evenly across the board. This is, as always, just a very loose guideline to the proportionate <i>representation</i> in the setting, which often contradicts canonical ratios (for a great example, 95% of Concordian fae are said to be Commoners. Unfortunately, 24% of all fae ever mentioned are Sidhe, and a full 40% of all changelings belong to a House and thus are not Commoner.)<br /> <br /> As of the close of 2003, there were 4211 Garou identified specifically by their tribe in the file. Of the Garou, the Get take first place at 10%, followed by the Uktena, Glass Walkers, Silver Fangs, Bone Gnawers and Fianna each at 8%, Children of Gaia and Black Furies at 7%, with the other tribes all bringing up the rear with 6% each - even the Stargazers, whose number of mentions in books is (largely through duplicate entries, I suspect) actually <i>higher</i> than their canonical population. 24% of the population are Ahrouns, 23% are Theurges, 19% Galliard, 18% Philodox, 17% ragabash - but we only have information on auspice for ~50% of the garou population. 51% are homid, 27% lupus, 22% metis, but there we only have ~30% information for specific garou births, and it doesn't include all RTs and GWs as Lupus and Homid (they aren't 100% either way, but for argument's sake let's assume they are) which bump the figures to a speculative 53% Homid, 32% Lupus, and 15% Metis. 593 of the changers in the list are specified as having died.<br /> <br /> Of the breeds, the Garou come in at 84% of all represented changers. Bastet come in with 4%, Mokole and Ratkin with 2%, and the rest all battle for 1 each with the exception of the Apis, the Ajaba, the Grondr, and the Camazotz who are statistically insignificant at 0% a pop.<br /> <br /> For an idea of how much caution needs to be taken with using these as anything but very rough guides until the dataset is finalized and cleaned up, I did a quick check on the vampire file. At present it hasn't had entries for multiples split into seperate entries, and there are a total of 680 entries with 2+ vampires and a cutoff of 29. There are also 54 entries dealing with nebulous 'dozens', 'hundreds', and 'thousands' as remarked on in various texts, for which both low and high end counts will necessarily differ. Similar problems apply across all lines. The population figure from just the count is 15,793. Add in just some of the higher-end references and it skyrockets to nearly 60,000 in terms of actual population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5307,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","user":"loomer","date":". 08-24-2016, 04:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T01:53:59-07:00","id":957473,"title":"","content":"Today, let's look at the changelings. The same caveats as for vampires and garou apply, though there are <i>many</i> more duplicate entries for changeling relative to total population size. We'll factor out the 10,000+ Mannikins or they'll utterly dominate the field.<br /> <br /> Of the Fae's 1245 entries, the sidhe are 24% of the total population. Trolls at 10%, Pooka at 9%, Eshu at 9%, Satyrs and Nockers at 8% each, Redcaps and Sluagh both at 7%, Boggan at 6%. Of the remaining 12%, Nunnehi and Menehune together make up 3%, and Merfolk and Selkies each take 1%. The rest may scrape a 1% here and there but are statistically insignificant in their representation. This is because many kith never had specific npcs mentioned. 31% of fae are specified as seelie and 16% are unseelie, with the shadow court at only 2%. Of the 419 with specific age categories, 18% (6% of the total figures) are children, 51% (17%) are Wilder, and 31% (10%) are grump. Most mentioned fae have no specified age category but fall into Wilder, as the 'default' age bracket, so if we like we can make those figures respectively 6%, 80%, and 10%.<br /> <br /> This really emphasizes the disproportinate representation, as mentioned above. 95% of fae are meant to be commoners - there <i>should</i> be another 5700 commoners to make that ratio hold true. Instead, the Sidhe dominate in the same way Ventrue do for Vampire. They have names, specific causes and personalities to the exclusion of other (usually more interesting) kiths.<br /> <br /> Of the Houses - and this is kind of shaky as often a single entry will include an 'ap &lt;x&gt;' and a designator of (House &lt;x&gt;) to make sure I don't miss it, but as it stands 41% of fae have a house designation (the figure for the necessary commoner population to bring it up to the correct ratio is 9600 more in that case.)<br /> Of them, Gwydion are 19%, Fiona 17%, Eiluned and Liam both 13%, Dougal 12%, Ailil 7%, Balor and Scathach 4%, Leanhaun 3%, and the rest - save for Varich at 1% - are all at 2%.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T13:49:05-07:00","id":958877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=956322#post956322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More demographics will be coming in the next few days. These are very rough figures and should only be considered to be loosely representative of rough breakdown by proportion, not of total populations. For an example of how rough this is, there are over 3000 indicators of direct sire-childe first-generation relationships, and in those cases my papers usually only list the clan once rather than both times.<br /> <br /> From a pool of 8801 entries, the clans make up the following proportions:<br /> Assamite: 4%<br /> Brujah: 10%<br /> Caitiff: 3%<br /> Cappadocian: 2%<br /> Gangrel: 8%<br /> Giovanni: 5%<br /> Lasombra: 6%<br /> Malkavian: 7%<br /> Nosferatu: 8%<br /> Ravnos: 3%<br /> Setite: 4%<br /> Toreador: 9%<br /> Tremere: 9%<br /> Tzimisce: 5%<br /> Ventrue: 11%<br /> Salubri: 1%<br /> Gargoyles: 1%<br /> Samedi: 1%<br /> Laibon (all lines): 1%<br /> All other bloodlines: 2%<br /> There is 1 ghoul for every 12 vampires recorded, and 1 in 10 vampires are diablerists.<br /> <br /> There are 3600 lineages that exend to first-degree relations (sire-childe), 1101 that extend to sire-grandchilde, 312 that extend to sire-ggc, 108 that extend to sire-gggc, 42 that extend to sire-ggggc, 10 that extend to sire-gggggc, and 2 that extend all the way to sire-ggggggc. That one is enough steps for, without diablerie or other shenanigans, one of those 2 to be 10th generation with an unbroken line from their antediluvian progenitor, with only one mention of clan in that entire list. In the worst case scenario, all ~5000 of those entries could significantly skew the results.</div> </div> </div> </div>No way there are those much salubri and cappadoci.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T21:38:58-07:00","id":959082,"title":"","content":"The figures include Dark Ages content. The Cappadocians were actually an incredibly populous clan then - quite possibly <i>the</i> most populous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T07:29:21-07:00","id":959233,"title":"","content":"Yes, and these are named vampires, so the true demographics are different. I would say that the list represents only 0.2% of the vampires that have existed since the Dark Ages, assuming an average existence of 10 years for most vampires before they meet destruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T07:35:11-07:00","id":959237,"title":"","content":"No, it includes unnamed vampires as well. I also don't know how you're deriving your 0.2% figure - perhaps you could explain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T20:36:47-07:00","id":962665,"title":"","content":"Well, let us assume that the average life expectancy of a vampire is 10 years. If we assume an average population of 1:50,000 Kindred within Europe, Asia, and the Americas, you would have had an average population of 5,000 within those regions over the past 1,000 years, depending on your estimations of the populations of those regions. The total population of vampires (active, destroyed, or in torpor), would have been 500,000 (14% of which are existent today). I guess I miscalculated beforehand, 8,800 vampires would be less than 2%, not 0.2%, of the total population of vampires who have existed over the last 1,000 years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T21:11:56-07:00","id":962680,"title":"","content":"Where are you getting the ten year mortality rate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T09:45:51-07:00","id":962856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=962680#post962680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where are you getting the ten year mortality rate?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It may be Sabbat, I know I've seen that 10 to 50 as most neonates just burn out and fall to the beast early. Becoming Ancilla is an accomplishment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T10:47:27-07:00","id":962885,"title":"","content":"I would say that it is a reasonable extrapolation. A large percentage of Kindred will be destroyed by their sires (or Princes) before they are released from supervision for being too dumb or too stubborn to maintain the Masquerade (in the Sabbat, shovelheads are designed to be disposable, so the majority of them will likely be destroyed during the first month of existence). I think that ten years is a good average because of the threats that neonates face. If they survive their first decade, I think that they can potentially survive for centuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T17:20:41-07:00","id":963008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=962885#post962885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that it is a reasonable extrapolation. A large percentage of Kindred will be destroyed by their sires (or Princes) before they are released from supervision for being too dumb or too stubborn to maintain the Masquerade (in the Sabbat, shovelheads are designed to be disposable, so the majority of them will likely be destroyed during the first month of existence). I think that ten years is a good average because of the threats that neonates face. If they survive their first decade, I think that they can potentially survive for centuries.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No I mean I'm sure I've seen a number like 10 to 50 years being the most common life expectency for a vampire in a vampire book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T23:06:41-07:00","id":963114,"title":"","content":"If that can be found I would very much appreciate it. There's a similar figure for Lasombra, but not for all cainites to my recollection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T11:04:00-07:00","id":963277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=963114#post963114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that can be found I would very much appreciate it. There's a similar figure for Lasombra, but not for all cainites to my recollection.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That may be where I read it and extrapolated. I can just remember &quot;its in a vampire book&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T11:39:37-07:00","id":963303,"title":"","content":"The Sabbat's average life expectancy is 25 years (which is rather optimistic).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T11:42:28-07:00","id":963306,"title":"","content":"I wonder if that includes shovelheads...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T12:26:57-07:00","id":963328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=963306#post963306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if that includes shovelheads...</div> </div> </div> </div>The way it is described, packs of 5 to 10 shovelheads (that have survived the burying) have 2-3 survivors the first night, then barely 1 survivor afterwards (if any). But exceptions aren't rare, whole packs sometimes manage to survive, and many Panders stem from those.<br /> <br /> But from my experience, shovelhead or no, it's impossible to reach 25 years without getting the 9 lives merit and groveling to the ST for more discipline dots.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T17:36:03-07:00","id":963468,"title":"","content":"I imagine that a very interesting chronicle would come from a pack of shovelheads surviving a conflict that drives the Sabbat from a city and having to survive as new vampires in hostile territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T17:42:21-07:00","id":963469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=963468#post963468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine that a very interesting chronicle would come from a pack of shovelheads surviving a conflict that drives the Sabbat from a city and having to survive as new vampires in hostile territory.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> best to make sure they are all of clans where they can't just fit in. Tzim, Lasombra, Pander, SoL","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T03:16:10-07:00","id":963615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=963468#post963468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine that a very interesting chronicle would come from a pack of shovelheads surviving a conflict that drives the Sabbat from a city and having to survive as new vampires in hostile territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, survival is an important theme for shovelheads. But more important is the regression.<br /> <br /> Most other Sabbat suffer regression, then take direction from sire, mentor, packmates, demons etc...But shovelheads usually have no one. They remain children with no morality, ethics or any sense of what's right or wrong. Most of the time, they can't make any sense or give any meaning to their actions.<br /> <br /> It's interesting to roleplay how such messed up people (if we can call them people at all) can mature on their own. For example:<br /> - A shovelhead diablerized several vampires. The hive of souls and memories make the shovelhead slowly build a personality that resembles his victims.<br /> - A shovelhead has Animalism/Auspex and by interacting through these disciplines starts gaining understanding of himself and his environment.<br /> <br /> well, things like that, I can't come up with elaborate scenarios.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T06:30:44-07:00","id":963663,"title":"","content":"You could have a pack get adopted by an elder vampire who may have a use for them. I can imagine a scenario where an Assamite sorcerer, perhaps a member of the Camarilla, could find a use for a vampire brute squad. The mentor would offer the hope of stability and a steady supply of animal blood in exchange for performing certain tasks for her behalf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T07:28:47-07:00","id":963684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=963663#post963663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could have a pack get adopted by an elder vampire who may have a use for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually the basic purpose of shovelheads. The brute squad idea is used a lot in Sabbat games, actually it's the typical scenario for 90% of Sabbat games (thanks to the 2e era), but I find it too simplistic and boring for a game...you know, too DnD for my taste.<br /> <br /> And making it a Camarilla brute squad doesn't really make it better. Though, it's more my inner DnD hater talking.<br /> <br /> Anyway, If I had to go the military path, I'd rather have them being adopted by a pack of Knights (Honorable Accord/Orion). The Knights would have them go through harsh training, ritae and initiations. They would test their abilities on crusades. Send them to infiltrate/investigate/spy Sabbat leaders, investigate assassinations and disappearances or dismantle Black Hand cells...<br /> <br /> One could also have a shovelhead be adopted by an Archon or a Baron. But I'm not very familiar with Camarilla/Anarch games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 09-05-2016, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T09:14:03-07:00","id":963730,"title":"","content":"Well, an abandoned shovelhead pack would not likely be adopted by Sabbat members if they were in a city recently captured by the Camarilla. An Archon would probably just go ahead and destroy them. In order for them to survive for long in a Camarilla city, you would really require two things. First, an elder who was willing to adopt them. Second, an elder who was powerful enough to say to the Prince 'Don't worry, I will keep them in line' and have the Prince believe it. An Assamite sorcerer who belonged to the Camarilla could fulfill both requirements.<br /> <br /> A brute squad does not necessarily mean something to provide target practice for a random 'hero'. Instead, it is a tool of assassination, intimidation, and sabotage. An Assamite sorcerer could send them on any number of missions which would be a waste of her talents, such as the assassination of mortal Infernalists or the industrial sabotage of the assets of a competitor.<br /> <br /> Of course, the question would be what could the Assamite sorcerer initially offer them in exchange for their loyalty. They would not understand the significance of an offer to lower their generation until later and a steady supply of animal blood only goes so far. Perhaps a chance to regain enough of their shattered Humanity to allow them to interact with their loved ones? I do not know...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T09:45:30-07:00","id":963745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=963730#post963730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps a chance to regain enough of their shattered Humanity to allow them to interact with their loved ones? I do not know...</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't keep enough of their memories to remember loved ones, unless they have Flashbacks or Hallucinations (but that doesn't really fix the issue).<br /> Supply of animal blood is no better than what Sabbat would do to them. Actually, Sabbat supply human to shovelheads, but I guess that's not the point of this discussion.<br /> <br /> I'd say simply having a father/mother figure sheltering them would be enough (since they suffer from regression and fits of terror).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 09-05-2016, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T09:47:39-07:00","id":963746,"title":"","content":"That could get rather Electra/Oedipus. I wonder if shovelheads are more or less likely than other vampires to diablerize their mother/father figure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T09:58:08-07:00","id":963754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954255-all-the-populations?p=963746#post963746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That could get rather Electra/Oedipus. I wonder if shovelheads are more or less likely than other vampires to diablerize their mother/father figure.</div> </div> </div> </div>well, if they get hungry or too unstable (frenzy), they may commit. I can think of one shovelhead: The Rose (Tzimisce) diablerized her sire right after she dug herself out of the grave.<br /> <br /> I don't know if they are more likely than other vampires to commit diablerie. Supposedly, megalomaniac vampires are the most likely to suck out the soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}